// REJECTS: Field 'tests' is required
//
// A serviceTestSuite may carry `data:` and MUST carry `tests:`. The grammar's suite body is
// `( serviceTestSuiteData | serviceTestSuiteTests )*` -- both optional, both repeatable --
// so a suite consisting of nothing but connection data parses cleanly and is refused only
// afterwards, by name.
//
// A suite with data and no tests is exactly what a half-written test file looks like, which
// is why a permissive rewrite would load it without complaint.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::SuiteWithoutTests
{
   pattern: '/x';
   documentation: 'd';
   execution: Single
   {
      query: |fixture::neg::Person.all();
      mapping: fixture::neg::M;
      runtime: fixture::neg::R;
   }
   testSuites:
   [
      suite1:
      {
         data:
         [
            connections:
            [
               c1:
                  ExternalFormat
                  #{
                     contentType: 'application/json';
                     data: '[]';
                  }#
            ]
         ]
      }
   ]
}
